{"kind":"request","text":"CE2 Card witness scope question. The existing late Card check resends once and receives Native expired. Its recursive check then sees terminal custody, so removing only card === undefined still would not call proof. To distinguish that guard at a reachable state, I propose strengthening the same existing Native Card case: one late check loses its exact-envelope resend before delivery, then the recursive resendExpired:false check remains expired and unresolved and must not invoke proof. A later deliberate check sends once and gets Native expired. Restart the McpService on the same custody before the late check. Assert exact original ACT bytes, zero new ACT signing, no helper/log proof and no unsent. No new case or deadline. Each check still sends at most once. May I use that sequence?","body":{"conditions":"Accept or narrow the proposed same-case lost-late-check then deliberate Native-answer check. It tests the recursive Card exclusion without fabricating custody state. No production resend policy or proof eligibility change is proposed.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}